verses.text:
Right away he followed her,
like an ox heading to the butcher,
like a fool walking into chains.{d}

I stood next to him like a skilled builder.{g}
Every day I was his delight.
I played in front of him all the time.

Proverbs of Solomon:{a}
Wise children make their father proud,
but foolish children bring their mother sorrow.

Even a poor person’s relatives hate him.
How much more his friends stay away!
He begs them with words, but they are gone.{a}

He is like a man counting the cost in his head.{c}
“Eat and drink!” he says to you,
but his heart is not with you.

Being invited to move up to a higher seat beats
being sent lower in front of a noble
whom your own eyes have seen.{b}

Churning milk makes butter.
Twisting a nose makes it bleed.
Stirring up anger makes a fight.{j}
